@startuml
title 4+1 Process View
skinparam shadowing false

start
:uvicorn starts FastAPI;\nPRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);
:JobManager.start() creates one worker\ntask per configured concurrency;
fork
  :React UI sends HTTP request;
  :FastAPI validates schema in the event loop;
  if (settings update?) then (yes)
    :Persist Setting row;
    :Add/retire worker tasks to match concurrency;
    :Rewrite DownloadOptions of queued/running/paused jobs;
    if (item currently downloading?) then (yes)
      :Mark item for runtime restart;
      :Current yt-dlp instance raises DownloadCancelled;
      :Requeue item (continuedl keeps the .part file);
    endif
  else (job action)
    :Create, pause, restart, delete, play, or open folder;
  endif
fork again
  :EventSource stays connected;
  :JobManager publishes + persists JobEvent;
  :UI refreshes GET /api/jobs;
end fork

if (queued item exists?) then (yes)
  :Worker dequeues JobItem id;
  :Claim lock checks state, then marks running;
  :Offload to a thread: asyncio.to_thread(_run_item_work);
  :prepare_download() resolves planned format/size;
  :yt-dlp downloads through the profile chain;
  :progress hook: StallGuard observes bytes;
  if (no new peak bytes within stall timeout?) then (yes)
    :raise DownloadStalled;\nitem fails with a readable reason;
  else (no)
    :ProgressPersistGate decides whether to write;
    :Aggregate substreams, then commit item + job totals;
  endif
  :Finish job only when no queued/running items remain;
else (no)
  :Worker waits on asyncio.Queue;
endif
:uvicorn stops;\nPRAGMA wal_checkpoint(TRUNCATE);
stop

note right
Each download runs in a worker thread,
so its progress hook uses its own
Session and commits on that thread.
end note
@enduml
